      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "WHY A SIXTH SURFACE",
      "originalText": "WHY A SIXTH SURFACE"
    },
    {
      "angle": 0,
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "index": "a078",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "updated": 1788261765240,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "seed": 617682,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8168862,
      "id": "el78",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 1088.36,
      "width": 630.0,
      "height": 78.12,
      "strokeColor": "#0f172a",
      "fontSize": 12.5,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "A repo's own method surfaces — its canon, PR rules, architecture review, procedures,\ndeep context — stay per-repo and unchanged. They cannot help a repo that has never seen\nthe lesson. The sixth surface holds only the cross-repo subset: org-scoped facts about the\nworld, enforced fail-closed at task time the way mechanical gates enforce at merge time.\nRepo quirks stay repo-scoped and never leak into anyone else's briefing.",
      "originalText": "A repo's own method surfaces — its canon, PR rules, architecture review, procedures,\ndeep context — stay per-repo and unchanged. They cannot help a repo that has never seen\nthe lesson. The sixth surface holds only the cross-repo subset: org-scoped facts about the\nworld, enforced fail-closed at task time the way mechanical gates enforce at merge time.\nRepo quirks stay repo-scoped and never leak into anyone else's briefing."
    },
